TI  - Interactions between forms of fat consumption and restaurant bread consumption
T2  - INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF OBESITY
AB  - How does fat consumption influence the consumption of companion foods such as bread? Adult restaurant goers who were randomly given olive oil for their bread used 26% more oil on each piece of bread compared to those who were given block butter, but they ended up eating 23% less bread in total. This finding illustrates one way in which fat intake can interact with the consumption of companion foods.
